TITLE: Creating NgRx Reducer Function with createReducer - TypeScript
DESCRIPTION: This snippet demonstrates how to create an NgRx reducer function using `createReducer`. It defines state transitions for a scoreboard, handling actions like `homeScore`, `awayScore`, `resetScore`, and `setScores` immutably by returning new state objects using the spread operator. It requires `initialState` and `ScoreboardPageActions` to be defined elsewhere.
SOURCE: https://github.com/ngrx/platform/blob/main/projects/ngrx.io/content/guide/store/reducers.md#_snippet_3

LANGUAGE: TypeScript
CODE:

```
export const scoreboardReducer = createReducer(
  initialState,
  on(ScoreboardPageActions.homeScore, state => ({ ...state, home: state.home + 1 })),
  on(ScoreboardPageActions.awayScore, state => ({ ...state, away: state.away + 1 })),
  on(ScoreboardPageActions.resetScore, state => ({ home: 0, away: 0 })),
  on(ScoreboardPageActions.setScores, (state, { game }) => ({ home: game.home, away: game.away }))
);
```

