TITLE: Handling Movie Loading with mapResponse in NgRx Effects (TypeScript)
DESCRIPTION: This NgRx effect, `loadMovies`, demonstrates the use of the `mapResponse` operator to handle the outcome of an API call. It listens for `MoviesPageActions.opened`, then uses `exhaustMap` to call `moviesService.getAll()`. The `mapResponse` operator then dispatches `MoviesApiActions.moviesLoadedSuccess` on successful data retrieval or `MoviesApiActions.moviesLoadedFailure` if an error occurs, providing a streamlined way to manage success and error states.
SOURCE: https://github.com/ngrx/platform/blob/main/projects/www/src/app/pages/guide/operators/operators.md#_snippet_3

LANGUAGE: TypeScript
CODE:

```
export const loadMovies = createEffect(
  (
    actions$ = inject(Actions),
    moviesService = inject(MoviesService)
  ) => {
    return actions$.pipe(
      ofType(MoviesPageActions.opened),
      exhaustMap(() =>
        moviesService.getAll().pipe(
          mapResponse({
            next: (movies) =>
              MoviesApiActions.moviesLoadedSuccess({ movies }),
            error: (error: { message: string }) =>
              MoviesApiActions.moviesLoadedFailure({
                errorMsg: error.message,
              }),
          })
        )
      )
    );
  },
  { functional: true }
);
```

