TITLE: Handling Errors in NgRx Effects for Movie Loading in TypeScript
DESCRIPTION: This effect demonstrates robust error handling for the movie loading process. It listens for the '[Movies Page] Load Movies' action and fetches movies. If `MoviesService#getAll()` encounters an error, the `catchError` operator dispatches a '[Movies API] Movies Loaded Error' action, ensuring the effect stream continues to run without terminating.
SOURCE: https://github.com/ngrx/platform/blob/main/projects/www/src/app/pages/guide/effects/index.md#_snippet_4

LANGUAGE: TypeScript
CODE:

```
import { Injectable, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { Actions, createEffect, ofType } from '@ngrx/effects';
import { of } from 'rxjs';
import { map, exhaustMap, catchError } from 'rxjs/operators';
import { MoviesService } from './movies.service';

@Injectable()
export class MoviesEffects {
  private actions$ = inject(Actions);
  private moviesService = inject(MoviesService);

  loadMovies$ = createEffect(() => {
    return this.actions$.pipe(
      ofType('[Movies Page] Load Movies'),
      exhaustMap(() =>
        this.moviesService.getAll().pipe(
          map((movies) => ({
            type: '[Movies API] Movies Loaded Success',
            payload: movies,
          })),
          catchError(() =>
            of({ type: '[Movies API] Movies Loaded Error' })
          )
        )
      )
    );
  });
}
```

